<title>NEW ZEALAND: CRICKET-ENGLAND WIN FIRST ONE-DAYER BY 4 WICKETS.</title>
<headline>CRICKET-ENGLAND WIN FIRST ONE-DAYER BY 4 WICKETS.</headline>
<dateline>CHRISTCHURCH, New Zealand 1997-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>England,</p>
<p>chasing a New Zealand total of 222, won by four wickets with</p>
<p>seven balls to spare in the first of five one-day internationals</p>
<p>on Thursday.</p>
<p>Score: New Zealand 222-6 (N.Astle 50, C.Harris 48 not out;</p>
<p>P.Tufnell 4-22), England 226-6 (G.Thorpe 82, A.Stewart 81;</p>
<p>H.Davis 3-44).</p>
</text>
